How can Prezent help customer success teams build impactful QBR and EBR presentations?

Prezent gives you access to a vast slide library and best-practice examples for QBRs and EBRs. You
can use AI to structure your content and auto-generate slides tailored to your goals. If you're
short on time, you can also use the expert overnight service to get a polished, on-brand deck by
morning.

Are there templates available for onboarding, training, and success plans?

Yes, Prezent provides a comprehensive library of templates designed for various Customer Success
needs, including onboarding, training, and success plans. These templates are customizable and
adhere to brand guidelines, allowing teams to efficiently create consistent and professional
presentations for different stages of the customer journey.

Can I personalize presentations for each customer while staying brand compliant?

Yes. You can personalize presentations by adding customer-specific goals, metrics, and content
directly into the slides. Prezent automatically applies your company’s brand guidelines—including
fonts, colors, layouts, and logo placement—through locked templates. You can also adjust the tone
and structure using Communication Fingerprint, so each presentation fits the audience while still
staying on-brand.

How does Prezent help reduce time spent on recurring customer presentations?

Prezent helps Customer Success teams save time by providing access to a Slide Library with over
35,000 pre-designed slides and more than 10,000 best-practice examples. The Presentation Library
acts as a centralized space where your team can store and reuse approved customer-facing decks You
can also use AI to auto-structure content and build new decks faster.

Can I turn my existing success decks into branded, consistent formats?

Yes. With the Transform feature, you can upload existing presentations and automatically apply your
company’s branding. Prezent will fix formatting, adjust layouts, and align everything to your
official template—saving time and improving consistency.

